t deployment frontend-proxy -n astronomy-shop -o yaml' to check for ConfigMap references. However, the user's available commands don't include that. Wait, the user can use 'exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd' with 'kubectl get deployment frontend-proxy -n astronomy-shop -o yaml' to get the deployment's YAML. \n\nSo the next step should be to check the deployment's YAML for any ConfigMap references. If the deployment is using a ConfigMap that's missing, that's the root cause. \n\nTherefore, the user should call 'exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd' with the command 'kubectl get deployment frontend-proxy -n astronomy-shop -o yaml' to inspect the deployment's configuration.\n</think>\n\n", additional_kwargs={'tool_calls': [{'function': {'arguments': '{"command": "kubectl get deployment frontend-proxy -n astronomy-shop -o yaml"}', 'name': 'exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-ba0db1d1b61c341f', 'type': 'function'}], 'provider_specific_fields': {'refusal': None, 'reasoning': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 1035, 'prompt_tokens': 6332, 'total_tokens': 7367, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'tool_calls', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfbfb-d98d-7fb2-8181-4bacdfb78e37-0', tool_calls=[{'name': 'exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd', 'args': {'command': 'kubectl get deployment frontend-proxy -n astronomy-shop -o yaml'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-ba0db1d1b61c341f', 'type': 'tool_call'}], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 6332, 'output_tokens': 1035, 'total_tokens': 7367}), ToolMessage(content='apiVersion: apps/v1\nkind: Deployment\nmetadata:\n  annotations:\n    deployment.kubernetes.io/revision: "1"\n    kubectl.kubernetes.io/last-applied-configuration: |\n      {"apiVersion":"apps/v1","kind":"Deployment","metadata":{"annotations":{"deployment.kubernetes.io/revision":"1","meta.helm.sh/release-name":"astronomy-shop","m