replaced with a new replica set (frontend-proxy-6df8c768f5). No action is required as this is an expected part of the Kubernetes rollout process."}', additional_kwargs={'provider_specific_fields': {'refusal': None, 'reasoning': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 300, 'prompt_tokens': 8482, 'total_tokens': 8782, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'stop', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfbfc-a7a0-7390-b4c4-bcf0193a6d31-0', tool_calls=[], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 8482, 'output_tokens': 300, 'total_tokens': 8782}), HumanMessage(content='Now generate a tool call according to your last chosen tool.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='b386745a-2220-4313-afce-ab87a6f1b97d'), AIMessage(content='<think>\nOkay, let me try to figure out what\'s going on here. The user is dealing with a Kubernetes cluster running the OpenTelemetry Demo Astronomy Shop application. They noticed that the frontend-proxy pod is in a Terminating state and wanted to diagnose if there\'s a fault.\n\nFirst, they started by checking the list of services using get_services, then looked into deployments and pods with kubectl commands. They found that the frontend-proxy pod was terminating, so they checked its logs and events. The logs didn\'t show any errors, and the metrics didn\'t indicate resource issues. The deployment rollout history showed a new replica set was created, which is part of a normal rollout process. \n\nThe user then considered network policies and ConfigMaps but didn\'t find any issues there. Since the pod is terminating as part of a planned rollout, there\'s no fault. The answer submitted explains that the termination is intentional and part of the deployment process, so no action is needed. \n\nSince the root cause is identified and the user has already submitted the answer, there\'s no need for further tool calls. The process should end here.\n</think>\n\nThe frontend-proxy pod\'s termination is part of a planned deployment rollout, as indicated by the `NewReplicaSetAvailable` status in the deployment conditions. No errors, resource exhaustion, or misconfigurations were found. The rollout is functioning as expected, and no faults require intervention. \n\nThe diagnosis is complete, and the root cause has been identified. No further tool calls are necessary. \n\n.submit_tool\n{"ans": "The frontend-proxy pod is terminating as part of a planned deployment rollout. There are no errors or faults causing the termination. The deployment is functioning normally, and the pod is being replaced with a new replica set (frontend-proxy-6df8c768f5). No action is required as this is an expected part of the Kubernetes rollout process."}', additional_kwargs={'provider_specific_fields': {'refusal': None, 'reasoning': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 387, 'prompt_tokens': 9466, 'total_tokens': 9853, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'stop', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfbfc-b65a-7961-a1c0-375dc89ae826-0', tool_calls=[], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 9466, 'output_tokens': 387, 'total_tokens': 9853}), HumanMessage(content='You are now in the thinking stage. Choose a tool from the available tools and justify your choice.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='8bea1c1c-db05-4939-9b5f-2bed21cee758'), AIMessage(content='<think>\nOkay, let me try to figure out what\'s going on here. The user is dealing with the OpenTelemetry Demo Astronomy Shop application, which is a microservices-based platform. They\'ve been trying to diagnose why the frontend-proxy pod is in a Terminating state. \n\nFirst, they started by checking the list of services using get_services, then looked at deployments and pods with kubectl commands. The pods seemed mostly healthy, but frontend-proxy was terminating. They checked the logs, deployment history, service configurations, and even network policies. \n\nThe key points from the tool responses were:\n- The frontend-proxy pod was in Terminating state but the deployment and service configs looked correct.\n- The deployment rollout history showed a new replica set was created.\n- The endpoints for the service were correctly pointing to the pod.\n- No errors in events or logs related to the pod\'s termination.\n- Metrics for CPU and memory didn\'t show any issues.\n\nPutting this together, the termination seems to be part of a planned rollout. The deployment is updating the replica set, so the old pod is being terminated normally. There\'s no fault here; it\'s just a regular Kubernetes rollout process. The user confirmed this by checking the deployment status and the new replica set. \n\nSince all checks indicate the termination is intentional and part of the rollout, there\'s no need for further actions. The root cause is the planned deployment, not a fault. So the final answer should state that the pod is terminating as expected during a rollout and no action is needed.\n</think>\n\n.submit_tool\n{"ans": "The frontend-proxy pod is terminating as part of a planned deployment rollout. There are no errors or faults causing the termination. The deployment is functioning normally, and the pod is being replaced with a new replica set (frontend-proxy-6df8c768f5). No action is required as this is an expected part of the Kubernetes rollout process."}', additional_kwargs={'provider_specific_fields': {'refusal': None, 'reasoning': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': Usage(completion_tokens=392, prompt_tokens=8771, total_tokens=9163, completion_tokens_details=None, prompt_tokens_details=None), 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'stop', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfbfc-c986-7