nctioning as expected, and no faults require intervention. \n\nThe diagnosis is complete, and the root cause has been identified. No further tool calls are necessary. \n\n.submit_tool\n{"ans": "The frontend-proxy pod is terminating as part of a planned deployment rollout. There are no errors or faults causing the termination. The deployment is functioning normally, and the pod is being replaced with a new replica set (frontend-proxy-6df8c768f5). No action is required as this is an expected part of the Kubernetes rollout process."}', additional_kwargs={'provider_specific_fields': {'refusal': None, 'reasoning': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 384, 'prompt_tokens': 9755, 'total_tokens': 10139, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'stop', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfbfc-dcd4-7210-8f31-e2447e0fe54a-0', tool_calls=[], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 9755, 'output_tokens': 384, 'total_tokens': 10139}), HumanMessage(content='You are now in the thinking stage. Choose a tool from the available tools and justify your choice.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='b2765468-1116-4347-abe8-d91c779b13db'), AIMessage(content='<think>\nOkay, let me try to figure out what\'s going on here. The user is dealing with the OpenTelemetry Demo Astronomy Shop application, which is a microservices-based platform. They\'ve been trying to diagnose why the frontend-proxy pod is in a Terminating state. \n\nFirst, they started by checking the list of services using get_services, then looked into deployments and pods with kubectl commands. They found that the frontend-proxy pod was terminating, so they checked its logs and events. The logs didn\'t show any errors, and the events indicated a rollout was happening. \n\nThey also checked the deployment\'s rollout history and found that a new replica set was being created. The service configuration seemed correct, and the endpoints were properly set. Metrics didn\'t show any resource issues. \n\nAfter all these checks, the conclusion was that the pod was being terminated as part of a planned rollout, not due to any fault. The user then submitted the answer, but the system kept prompting for more tool calls. \n\nWait, maybe the system is expecting a final confirmation. Since the root cause was identified as a normal rollout, and no faults were found, the correct action is to stop the diagnosis. The user has already submitted the answer, so the final step is to ensure that the submission is correctly formatted and that no further actions are needed. \n\nThe user might have submitted the answer multiple times, but the system is still asking for a tool call. However, since the root cause is clear and no further issues are detected, the appropriate response is to confirm the diagnosis and stop the process. Therefore, the final answer should restate that the termination is part of a rollout and no action is required.\n</think>\n\n.submit_tool\n{"ans": "The frontend-proxy pod is terminating as part of a planned deployment rollout. There are no errors or faults causing the termination. The deployment is functioning normally, and the pod is being replaced with a new replica set (frontend-proxy-6df8c768f5). No action is required as this is an expected part of the Kubernetes rollout process."}', additional_kwargs={'provider_specific_fields': {'refusal': None, 'reasoning': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 424, 'prompt_tokens': 9060, 'total_tokens': 9484, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'stop', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfbfc-efe3-7f20-9b9d-fbcc94976bcc-0', tool_calls=[], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 9060, 'output_tokens': 424, 'total_tokens': 9484}), HumanMessage(content='Now generate a tool call according to your last chosen tool.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='c7fcfe25-0256-4f98-9336-5419cfa797ea'), AIMessage(content='<think>\nOkay, let me try to figure out what\'s going on here. The user is dealing with a Kubernetes cluster running the OpenTelemetry Demo Astronomy Shop application. They noticed that the frontend-proxy pod is in a Terminating state and want to diagnose why.\n\nFirst, they checked the pods and deployments, which showed that the frontend-proxy deployment has a replica set being rolled out. The service configuration looked correct, and the endpoints were properly set. They also checked the ConfigMaps and didn\'t find any issues there. \n\nNext, they looked into metrics for CPU and memory usage, but there were no data points, which might mean the metrics aren\'t being collected properly or the query was incorrect. Then, they tried to get logs from the terminating pod, but the logs weren\'t available. \n\nThe key clue came from the deployment\'s status showing "NewReplicaSetAvailable," which indicates a rolling update is happening. The old pod is being replaced by a new replica set. Since there were no errors in the logs or metrics, and the deployment is progressing as expected, the termination is part of a normal rollout. \n\nSo, the root cause is that the frontend-proxy pod is being terminated as part of a planned deployment rollout. There\'s no fault here; it\'s just a normal Kubernetes operation. The user doesn\'t need to take any action since the rollout is expected and the deployment is functioning correctly.\n</think>\n\nThe frontend-proxy pod\'s termination is part of a planned deployment rollout, as indicated by the `NewReplicaSetAvailable` status in the deployment conditions. No errors, resource exhaustion, or misconfigurations were found. The rollout is functioning as expected, and no faults require intervention. \n\nThe diagnosis is complete, and the root cause has been identified. No further tool calls are necessary. \n\n.submit_tool\n{"ans": "The frontend-proxy pod is terminating as part of a planned deployment rollout. There are no errors or faults causing the termination. The deployment is functioning normally, and the pod is being replaced with a new replica set (frontend-proxy-6df8c768f5). No action is required as this is an expected part of the Kubernetes rollout process."}', additional_kwargs={'provider_specific_fields': {'refusal': None, 'reasoning': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 444, 'prompt_tokens': 10044, 'total_tokens': 10488, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'stop', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfbfd-04ce-7491-a612-4f238ce44b3c-0', tool_calls=[], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 10044, 'output_tokens': 444, 'total_tokens': 10488}), HumanMessage(content='You are now in the thinking stage. Choose a tool from the available tools and justify your choice.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='9006c543-f399-4aa9-9402-6b02cf65ba2a')]]
