n identified. No further tool calls are necessary. \n\n.submit_tool\n{"ans": "The frontend-proxy pod is terminating as part of a planned deployment rollout. There are no errors or faults causing the termination. The deployment is functioning normally, and the pod is being replaced with a new replica set (frontend-proxy-6df8c768f5). No action is required as this is an expected part of the Kubernetes rollout process."}', additional_kwargs={'provider_specific_fields': {'refusal': None, 'reasoning': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 444, 'prompt_tokens': 10044, 'total_tokens': 10488, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'stop', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfbfd-04ce-7491-a612-4f238ce44b3c-0', tool_calls=[], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 10044, 'output_tokens': 444, 'total_tokens': 10488}), HumanMessage(content='You are now in the thinking stage. Choose a tool from the available tools and justify your choice.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='9006c543-f399-4aa9-9402-6b02cf65ba2a'), AIMessage(content='<think>\nOkay, let me try to figure out what\'s going on here. The user is dealing with the OpenTelemetry Demo Astronomy Shop application, which is a microservices-based platform. They\'ve noticed that the frontend-proxy pod is in a Terminating state, and they\'re trying to diagnose why.\n\nFirst, they checked the list of services using get_services, which gave them all the service names. Then they looked at the pods and deployments with kubectl commands. The frontend-proxy pod was in Terminating, but the deployment and service configurations seemed okay. They checked the logs, events, and rollout history, but didn\'t find any errors. The metrics didn\'t show resource issues either.\n\nThe key clue here is the deployment\'s rollout history. The status shows a NewReplicaSetAvailable, which means a new version of the deployment is being rolled out. The old pod is being terminated as part of the rollout process. Since the deployment is healthy and the new replica set is available, the termination is intentional and part of the normal update process. There\'s no fault here; it\'s just a planned update. So the root cause is the deployment rollout, not a failure.\n</think>\n\n.submit_tool\n{"ans": "The frontend-proxy pod is terminating as part of a planned deployment rollout. There are no errors or faults causing the termination. The deployment is functioning normally, and the pod is being replaced with a new replica set (frontend-proxy-6df8c768f5). No action is required as this is an expected part of the Kubernetes rollout process."}', additional_kwargs={'provider_specific_fields': {'refusal': None, 'reasoning': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 319, 'prompt_tokens': 9349, 'total_tokens': 9668, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'stop', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfbfd-1ad4-7133-b6f1-0a369c4a2a3b-0', tool_calls=[], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 9349, 'output_tokens': 319, 'total_tokens': 9668}), HumanMessage(content='Now generate a tool call according to your last chosen tool.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='ae7908cc-f173-4cd5-8c37-f3f49f9cc821'), AIMessage(content='<think>\nOkay, let me try to figure out what\'s going on here. The user is dealing with a Kubernetes cluster running the OpenTelemetry Demo Astronomy Shop application. They noticed that the frontend-proxy pod is in a Terminating state and want to diagnose why.\n\nFirst, they checked the pods and deployments, which showed that the frontend-proxy pod was terminating, but the deployment was healthy. Then they looked into the service configuration, endpoints, and network policies, all of which seemed okay. They also checked the logs and metrics but didn\'t find any errors or resource issues.\n\nThe key clue came from the deployment\'s status showing a "NewReplicaSetAvailable" condition, which indicates a rollout is happening. The pod is being replaced as part of a new version deployment. Since there were no errors in the logs or metrics, and the deployment is progressing normally, the termination is intentional. \n\nSo the root cause is that the frontend-proxy pod is being terminated as part of a planned deployment rollout. There\'s no fault here; it\'s just a normal part of Kubernetes updating the service. The user doesn\'t need to take any action since the rollout is expected and the system is functioning correctly.\n</think>\n\nThe frontend-proxy pod\'s termination is part of a planned deployment rollout, as indicated by the `NewReplicaSetAvailable` status in the deployment conditions. No errors, resource exhaustion, or misconfigurations were found. The rollout is functioning as expected, and no faults require intervention. \n\nThe diagnosis is complete, and the root cause has been identified. No further tool calls are necessary. \n\n.submit_tool\n{"ans": "The frontend-proxy pod is terminating as part of a planned deployment rollout. There are no errors or faults causing the termination. The deployment is functioning normally, and the pod is being replaced with a new replica set (frontend-proxy-6df8c768f5). No action is required as this is an expected part of the Kubernetes rollout process."}', additional_kwargs={'provider_specific_fields': {'refusal': None, 'reasoning': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 400, 'prompt_tokens': 10333, 'total_tokens': 10733, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'stop', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfbfd-2aac-77a0-807f-8e271326900a-0', tool_calls=[], invalid_tool_calls=[], 