laced with a new replica set (frontend-proxy-6df8c768f5). No action is required as this is an expected part of the Kubernetes rollout process."}', additional_kwargs={'provider_specific_fields': {'refusal': None, 'reasoning': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 444, 'prompt_tokens': 10044, 'total_tokens': 10488, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'stop', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfbfd-04ce-7491-a612-4f238ce44b3c-0', tool_calls=[], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 10044, 'output_tokens': 444, 'total_tokens': 10488}), HumanMessage(content='You are now in the thinking stage. Choose a tool from the available tools and justify your choice.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='9006c543-f399-4aa9-9402-6b02cf65ba2a'), AIMessage(content='<think>\nOkay, let me try to figure out what\'s going on here. The user is dealing with the OpenTelemetry Demo Astronomy Shop application, which is a microservices-based platform. They\'ve noticed that the frontend-proxy pod is in a Terminating state, and they\'re trying to diagnose why.\n\nFirst, they checked the list of services using get_services, which gave them all the service names. Then they looked at the pods and deployments with kubectl commands. The frontend-proxy pod was in Terminating, but the deployment and service configurations seemed okay. They checked the logs, events, and rollout history, but didn\'t find any errors. The metrics didn\'t show resource issues either.\n\nThe key clue here is the deployment\'s rollout history. The status shows a NewReplicaSetAvailable, which means a new version of the deployment is being rolled out. The old pod is being terminated as part of the rollout process. Since the deployment is healthy and the new replica set is available, the termination is intentional and part of the normal update process. There\'