ew version deployment. Since there were no errors in the logs or metrics, and the deployment is progressing normally, the termination is intentional. \n\nSo the root cause is that the frontend-proxy pod is being terminated as part of a planned deployment rollout. There\'s no fault here; it\'s just a normal part of Kubernetes updating the service. The user doesn\'t need to take any action since the rollout is expected and the system is functioning correctly.\n</think>\n\nThe frontend-proxy pod\'s termination is part of a planned deployment rollout, as indicated by the `NewReplicaSetAvailable` status in the deployment conditions. No errors, resource exhaustion, or misconfigurations were found. The rollout is functioning as expected, and no faults require intervention. \n\nThe diagnosis is complete, and the root cause has been identified. No further tool calls are necessary. \n\n.submit_tool\n{"ans": "The frontend-proxy pod is terminating as part of a planned deployment rollout. There are no errors or faults causing the termination. The deployment is functioning normally, and the pod is being replaced with a new replica set (frontend-proxy-6df8c768f5). No action is required as this is an expected part of the Kubernetes rollout process."}', additional_kwargs={'provider_specific_fields': {'refusal': None, 'reasoning': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 400, 'prompt_tokens': 10333, 'total_tokens': 10733, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'stop', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfbfd-2aac-77a0-807f-8e271326900a-0', tool_calls=[], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 10333, 'output_tokens': 400, 'total_tokens': 10733}), HumanMessage(content='You are now in the thinking stage. Choose a tool from the available tools and justify your choice.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='25881bf5-ffa2-4a29-