ocess."}', additional_kwargs={'provider_specific_fields': {'refusal': None, 'reasoning': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 394, 'prompt_tokens': 9638, 'total_tokens': 10032, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'stop', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfbfd-3e96-7273-97f5-984dcdd41eec-0', tool_calls=[], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 9638, 'output_tokens': 394, 'total_tokens': 10032}), HumanMessage(content='Now generate a tool call according to your last chosen tool.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='eeed3536-0a5a-4dde-9a97-c00a9e41f835'), AIMessage(content='<think>\nOkay, let me try to figure out what\'s going on here. The user is dealing with a Kubernetes cluster running the OpenTelemetry Demo Astronomy Shop application. They noticed that the frontend-proxy pod is in a Terminating state and want to diagnose why.\n\nFirst, they checked the pods and deployments, which showed that the frontend-proxy deployment had a new replica set being created. The service configuration looked correct, and the endpoints were properly set. They also checked the ConfigMaps and didn\'t find any issues there. Metrics for CPU and memory didn\'t show any problems, and the logs from the previous pod didn\'t have errors.\n\nThe key clue here is the deployment\'s status showing "NewReplicaSetAvailable," which indicates a rolling update is happening. The old pod is being terminated to make way for the new version. Since there are no errors in the logs or metrics, the termination is likely part of the planned rollout. The user might be concerned because the pod is terminating, but it\'s a normal part of Kubernetes\' rolling update process. The answer should confirm that this is an expected behavior and no action is needed.\n</think>\n\n.submit_tool\n{"ans": "The frontend-proxy pod is terminating as part of 