ory usage, but the results were empty, which might mean the metrics aren\'t being collected or there\'s no data. Finally, they tried to get the previous logs of the terminating pod, which might have contained the reason for termination. \n\nAfter all these checks, the conclusion was that the pod was terminating as part of a planned rollout, and there were no faults. The user has been submitting the same answer multiple times, which suggests they\'re confident in their diagnosis. Since the system allows up to 20 rounds and they\'ve already used several, it\'s time to finalize the answer.\n</think>\n\n.submit_tool\n{"ans": "The frontend-proxy pod is terminating as part of a planned deployment rollout. There are no errors or faults causing the termination. The deployment is functioning normally, and the pod is being replaced with a new replica set (frontend-proxy-6df8c768f5). No action is required as this is an expected part of the Kubernetes rollout process."}', additional_kwargs={'provider_specific_fields': {'refusal': None, 'reasoning': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': Usage(completion_tokens=381, prompt_tokens=9848, total_tokens=10229, completion_tokens_details=None, prompt_tokens_details=None), 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'stop', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfbfd-619d-7092-af8b-c1ff8dfe3bc6-0', tool_calls=[], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 9848, 'output_tokens': 381, 'total_tokens': 10229}), HumanMessage(content='Now generate a tool call according to your last chosen tool.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='95ec4f8b-0495-4d98-9cf5-3b7802b41f3a')]]
